en the  visuals would have been crafted by dan  o'bannon and h.r gieger most famous for  the nightmarish designs of ridley  scott's alien finally perhaps most  impressively the film's soundtrack would  have been performed in part by legendary  rock band pink floyd unfortunately  jodorowsky's vision proved too  unfeasible for any major studio and the  adaptation rights were eventually sold  off they were picked up by italian  producer dino de laurentiis resulting in  david lynch's now infamous adaptation  from 1984.  stanley kubrick is a name synonymous  with both cinematic brilliance and  problematic genius kubrick was a master  of pushing the art of cinema to its most  absurd possibilities into breathtaking  results on the flip side he was known  for a harsh and borderline abusive  attitude when directing his films  especially toward his actors for all his  legendary work kubrick wasn't always  successful with his cinematic  undertakings case in point his most  notable cancelled film napoleon after  rapping on 2001 a space odyssey kubrick  looked to direct a sizably budgeted film  about french emperor napoleon bonaparte  kubrick had an active fascination with  the historical figure that dated back to  his early childhood obsessed with making  the film as accurate as possible kubrick  insisted on watching every previous  napoleon film available he even went as  far as to replicate napoleon's real life  diet in order to fully immerse himself  in bonaparte's habits and mindset the  film much like kubrick's other works  would have been predicated heavily on  immense detail from the sets to the  costumes it was a project that kubrick  was truly passionate about pauline is  still in his grave  waiting to be brought back to life sadly  due to the prohibitive cost of shooting  on location as well as the box office  disappointment of 1970s waterloo the  project was scrapped it was a  disappointing end to what could have  been one of the greatest period war  films and character studies ever put to  celluloid  pixar is one of the most successful  names in mainstream animation and it's  impossible not to see why with films  like the toy story series finding nemo  up and countless others the studio has  captivated countless children and adults  however there was one pixar project that  was apparently immune to the studio's  magic the film newt would have followed  the last remaining male and female  blue-footed nukes a duo forced to work  together to repopulate their species  even though they can't stand each other  clearly the project had lots of  potential for comedy and heart but that  wasn't enough to get it off the ground  the film's development remained very  stagnant in the years following its 2008  announcement and a few years later it  was officially announced that newt had  been scrapped by pixar making it the  only film in the studio's history to be  announced and later canceled it's  unclear what the true death blow was for  newt because there were actually several  likely contributing factors the most  likely reason was its similarities to  another animated film that was in  production at the time blue sky studios  rio  universal pictures correctly flagging  e.t the extraterrestrial as a surefire  hit approached steven spielberg about a  sequel shortly before the original's  release spielberg usually known for not  doing sequels expressed interest and  developed a nine-page treatment for a  follow-up this treatment which has been  available online for years was titled  et2 nocturnal fears nocturnal fears  would have followed the core cast from  the original contending with another far  deadlier alien encounter a mutated  faction of e.t species would abduct  elliott along with his friends at the  climax of the film et would make a  dramatic return to vanquish the evil  aliens and save his earthling friends  nocturnal fears was written to be a more  mature story a far cry from the  family-friendly nature of the original  this i