 so utterly dedicated  to your vision that you'll never give up  del toro is best known for creating  lavish settings and otherworldly  creatures that nearly defied description  as we've seen in his genre bending films  like pan's labyrinth and his best  picture winner the shape of water del  toro has been making visionary films for  decades and shows no signs of slowing  down h.p lovecraft's 1931 novella at the  mountains of madness is the tale of a  group of explorers stranded in the  antarctic who are slowly picked off one  by one by an otherworldly terror it's  not surprising that del toro fought long  and hard to helm the first adaptation of  the horrific tale the pet project was  announced over a decade ago but nothing  has materialized since much to the  disappointment of del toro himself the  eventual cancellation of the project  stemmed from a few factors most notably  disputes over the film's rating while  universal studios was dead set on a  pg-13 rating del toro stuck to his guns  and continually push for an r-rated film  del toro has gone on record saying the  mpaa rating issue was the nail in the  coffin for the project that's too bad as  it would have likely been one of the  best adaptations of any lovecraft story  to date  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you

